{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cuddlesome-amoral-oyster","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nF47 is approved as research. The legacy ticket wordlist is byte-stable but lacks an established upstream revision or license. The import commit names Digital Service Orchestra without recording a source or terms.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Record the current digest, line count, size, and introduction commit.\n- Examine primary-source history and upstream candidates.\n- Record retrieval details, comparison methods, and results.\n- Classify provenance and license as proven, disproven, or unresolved.\n- Propose any supported repository correction separately.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The ticket records the digest, line count, size, and introduction commit.\n- [ ] Every primary source examined has a retrieval date, comparison method, and match result.\n- [ ] The conclusion classifies source and license evidence.\n- [ ] No attribution or license claim is made without primary-source proof.\n- [ ] Any repository correction is proposed separately for approval.\n- [ ] The wordlist, aliases, documentation, NOTICE, and distribution metadata remain unchanged.","id":"1b8b-fa85-b280-42ee","parent_id":"2bce-d81d-0eed-42e5","priority":2,"tags":["documentation","research","F47"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Research legacy wordlist provenance without attribution claims"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787590191693644001,"uuid":"21220a7e-3488-4e34-9a77-381916eac3db"}